---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ProjectNavigation from "../../components/ProjectNavigation.astro";
import { appsBySlug, person } from "../../data/site";
---
<BaseLayout title="Smart Strap Local" description="Personal WHOOP 5.0 companion project: planned direct Bluetooth to iPhone and local storage. App development and hardware validation pending." path="/apps/strap-local">
  <article class="container prose">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="page-header__kicker">iPhone · Personal, noncommercial use · In development</p>
      <h1 class="page-header__title">Smart Strap Local</h1>
      <p class="page-header__lead">A personal iPhone companion for your WHOOP 5.0. The plan: connect directly over Bluetooth and keep your measurements on your phone.</p>
      <div class="page-header__actions"><a href={appsBySlug["strap-local"].briefUrl}>Project notes ↗</a></div>
    </header>

    <aside class="project-status">
      <strong>Project setup · hardware validation pending</strong>
      <p>No app download or verified device connection is available yet. The next milestone is proving pairing and data access on the owner's strap.</p>
    </aside>
    <dl class="project-facts" aria-label="Project at a glance">
      <div><dt>Hardware</dt><dd>WHOOP 5.0</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Phone</dt><dd>iPhone</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Connection plan</dt><dd>Direct Bluetooth</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <ProjectNavigation links={[
      { label: "Connection plan", href: "#connection" },
      { label: "Validation", href: "#validation" },
      { label: "Privacy & use", href: "#privacy" },
      { label: "Rights concerns", href: "#rights" },
    ]} />

    <h2 id="connection">A direct local connection</h2>
    <p>The planned native app connects the strap to a nearby iPhone over Bluetooth Low Energy. Available measurements would be stored and analyzed locally, without a vendor cloud API, subscription, cloud relay or required Mac.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Pair directly with the strap using the iPhone's Bluetooth.</li>
      <li>Show available live readings with timestamps and freshness.</li>
      <li>Reconnect after range loss and retrieve missed device history where supported.</li>
      <li>Keep measurements and analysis on the iPhone.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Some measurements may arrive as device history rather than a live stream. Background collection depends on iOS, firmware and what the device exposes. This page describes the project; device connection requires the planned native app.</p>

    <h2 id="validation">What needs to be proven</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Reliable pairing and authenticated access on WHOOP 5.0.</li>
      <li>Correct units and timestamps, with unsupported measurements identified.</li>
      <li>Repeatable synchronization without duplicate or silently missing samples.</li>
      <li>Reconnect and catch-up after phone locking, app interruption or range loss.</li>
    </ul>
    <details class="project-details">
      <summary>Technical approach &amp; references</summary>
      <p>NOOP is the initial app candidate under PolyForm Noncommercial. Its WHOOP 5.0 support is experimental; authenticated history access and overnight inputs still need validation on the actual firmware. Live heart rate alone does not establish those capabilities.</p>
      <p>GenieMax is an MIT analytics and decoder reference; its public package excludes transport and a full app UI. HRV, sleep, recovery, respiration, temperature and SpO2 remain unverified for this personal build.</p>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/ryanbr/noop" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOOP app reference</a> · <a href="https://github.com/satayutata/geniemax-core" rel="noopener noreferrer">GenieMax analytics reference</a>. Preserve upstream licenses and attribution.</p>
    </details>

    <h2 id="privacy">Privacy and intended use</h2>
    <p>A personal, noncommercial experiment with owned hardware. No sale, public app release or hosted health-data service is planned. Local storage, protected authentication keys and a delete-data control are requirements awaiting implementation.</p>

    <h2>Independence and responsibility</h2>
    <p>Independent and unofficial. Not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by or supported by WHOOP, Inc. The hardware name identifies intended compatibility; its owner retains the trademark.</p>
    <p>Experimental wellness information, not a medical device or a substitute for professional care. Provided as-is without warranties; liability is disclaimed to the extent permitted by applicable law. Compatibility, accuracy and freedom from third-party claims are not guaranteed. Personal use and these notices do not override applicable law, agreements or third-party licenses.</p>

    <h2 id="rights">Rights concerns and takedown requests</h2>
    <p>The project owner intends to honor takedown requests from WHOOP or an authorized rights holder by promptly disabling or removing identified public materials while reviewing the concern. Please include the affected URL or material, the right asserted and your authority to act.</p>
    <p><a href={`mailto:${person.email}?subject=Smart%20Strap%20Local%20rights%20concern`}>Contact about Smart Strap Local</a></p>
    <div class="links-row"><a href={appsBySlug["strap-local"].briefUrl}>Project notes</a><a href="/#projects">All projects</a></div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
